Controller navigation is the only input a console has

`ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad` is set only when `CVAR_IMGUI_CONTROLLER_NAV` is on
*and* the menu or menubar is visible, and cleared every frame otherwise. On a desktop
that is a sensible default: the pad drives the menu when asked to, and anything else is
answered with a mouse.

There is no mouse here, and both conditions fail for reasons unrelated to intent. The
CVar defaults to 0. And the first thing a player meets is not the menubar - it is
`InitOTR`'s "No O2R files found. Generate one now?", a popup, so
`GetMenuOrMenubarVisible()` is false. The `else` branch then clears the flag on every
frame the dialog is up.

What that produced was a title that looked finished and was not: the prompt on screen
with Yes and No, a software cursor that does not move, and no way to reach either
button - while the pad was connected and SDL was reporting it as joystick 0. There is
nothing to fall back to, so on this platform the flag is simply on.

Both places are patched, and the second is the one that matters: the first is set once
at init, the per-frame copy in the draw path is what was undoing it.

diff --git a/libultraship/src/ship/window/gui/Gui.cpp b/libultraship/src/ship/window/gui/Gui.cpp
index 426a965..d7c2cf4 100644
--- a/libultraship/src/ship/window/gui/Gui.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/ship/window/gui/Gui.cpp
@@ -129,12 +129,25 @@ void Gui::Init(GuiWindowInitData windowImpl) {
         mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_ViewportsEnable;
     }
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    // A console has no mouse, so controller navigation is not a preference here - it is the
+    // only way anything on screen can be answered. Both conditions below fail on this
+    // platform for reasons that have nothing to do with intent: the CVar defaults to 0, and
+    // the first thing a player meets is a popup rather than the menubar, so
+    // `GetMenuOrMenubarVisible()` is false. The `else` then clears the flag every frame.
+    //
+    // What that looked like: "No O2R files found. Generate one now?" with Yes and No, a
+    // cursor that does not move, and no way to reach either button - while the pad was
+    // connected and SDL was reporting it.
+    mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad;
+#else
     if (Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetConsoleVariables()->GetInteger(CVAR_IMGUI_CONTROLLER_NAV, 0) &&
         GetMenuOrMenubarVisible()) {
         mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad;
     } else {
         mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags &= ~ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad;
     }
+#endif
 
     GetGuiWindow("Stats")->Init();
     GetGuiWindow("Input Editor")->Init();
@@ -544,12 +557,19 @@ void Gui::DrawMenu() {
             GetMenuBar()->ToggleVisibility();
         }
         Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetWindow()->GetMouseStateManager()->UpdateMouseCapture();
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        /* Kept on for the reason given where it is first set: there is no mouse here, so
+         * clearing this leaves nothing that can reach a button. This is the per-frame copy,
+         * and it is the one that was undoing it. */
+        mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad;
+#else
         if (Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetConsoleVariables()->GetInteger(CVAR_IMGUI_CONTROLLER_NAV, 0) &&
             GetMenuOrMenubarVisible()) {
             mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad;
         } else {
             mImGuiIo->ConfigFlags &= ~ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad;
         }
+#endif
     }
 
     // Mac interprets this as cmd+r when io.ConfigMacOSXBehavior is on (on by default)
